ale-cache artifact. EXCLUDED: All Bedding, Mattresses (mattress itself is not a textile product - only Mattress Pads & Toppers / Mattress Covers & Protectors under 'Bedding Essentials' are), Curtain Rings & Brackets / Curtain Poles & Accessories / Shower Curtain Rods (hardware, not textile); Extra Small/Small/Medium/Large/Extra Large/Oversized Rugs (redundant size-filtered views of All Rugs, not distinct product-type categories, matching SR1 wayfair.com precedent); Rug Grippers (underlay accessory, not the rug itself); Bookcases, Cabinets & Chests, Ottomans/Pouffes & Footstools (listed under the Storage mega-menu's 'Storage Furniture' group but their actual hrefs resolve to /furniture/... - site's own canonical hierarchy places them in Furniture scope, confirmed by direct URL inspection); Wall Hooks under Storage (also resolves to the same /furniture/ URL as the Hallway Furniture & Storage menu's Wall Hooks); Countertop & Sink Organisation cluster (Paper Towel & Napkin Holders, Spoon Rests, Utensil Holders, Dish Racks & Drying Mats, Knife Blocks & Storage, Mug Trees - kitchenware/utensil accessories, not storage/organization products per the Kitchen & Dining boundary); Countertop Bath Accessories (page title confirms 'Toothbrush Holder Set' - decorative bathroom accessories, not storage); All Vacuums, Ironing Boards, Clothes Drying Racks, Rubbish Bins & Recycling Bins (Cleaning & Laundry group items explicitly excluded by storage.md); Dog Food Storage & Treat Jars, Litter Boxes (Pet-scope products, kept out for consistency with SR1 which excluded all pet storage). Blinds & Shades was included at LOW confidence with a MANUAL REVIEW flag because the single aggregate category page title itself reads 'Blinds - Roller, Roman, Vertical & Venetian' - Roman/Roller are textile per rules but Vertical/Venetian are typically hard slat materials, and the site provides no way to view them split apart. Summer Houses, Log Cabins, Shower & Bathtub Accessories, Baby & Kids Bookcases,